# tepna-capture — systemd/99-tepna-btattach-hotplug.rules
# Copyright 2026 Michal Planicka · SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# A REPLUGGED ZEPHYR BOARD MUST ATTACH AGAIN BY ITSELF (residue
# 2026-11-01-a-replugged-zephyr-board-keeps-its-old-tty; BOX-EVENING-2026-10-26-BRIEF.md §6 T1).
# `tepna-btattach@<usb-serial>.service` holds a line discipline on the tty it was handed at start. A
# board that is unplugged and plugged back in gets a NEW ttyACM number from the kernel, so the old
# instance stays active on a device that no longer exists and the radio never rejoins the failover
# ladder. The owner restarted that unit by hand twice on 2026-11-01.
#
# WHAT THIS RULE ADDS. Every matching tty gets a stable name at /dev/tepnabt/<usb-serial>, and udev
# asks systemd to start that serial's attach instance. The companion drop-in
# `tepna-btattach-bind-to-tty.conf` binds the instance to that named device, so the unit stops when the
# board leaves and starts again when it comes back.
#
# WHY THE MODEL GLOB. The same vendor id also covers a board flashed with the nRF Sniffer image, which
# is no HCI controller and must never get an attach unit. Only the `hci_usb` firmware carries `HCI` in
# its model string (see deploy/flash-nrf52840-hci.sh).
#
# WHY THE SERIAL GLOB. The instance name IS the USB serial, so a board that reports no serial would
# instance the unit under an empty name. One glob keeps that case away from systemd.
#
# WHY `ACTION!="remove"` RATHER THAN `ACTION=="add"`. A `bind` or a `change` event on a tty that is
# already present must reach the same path, and only the removal has nothing to start.
#
# Installed by deploy/check-system-files.sh, which byte-compares it against /etc. A udev reload applies
# to FUTURE events only, so installing this file never disturbs a running capture.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="tty", KERNEL=="ttyACM*", ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="2fe3", ENV{ID_MODEL}=="*HCI*", ENV{ID_SERIAL_SHORT}=="?*", SYMLINK+="tepnabt/$env{ID_SERIAL_SHORT}", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="tepna-btattach@$env{ID_SERIAL_SHORT}.service"
